inor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Wabash River at Vincennes.\n\n* WHEN...Until Sunday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 18.0 feet, Agricultural lands and some oil fields\nflood.  Several township roads about 1.25 miles south of St.\nFrancesville and River Road between Billett Road and Lincoln\nMemorial Bridge in Lawrence County are flooded.  Extensive flooding\nof Kimmell Park at Vincennes.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:45 PM CDT /8:45 PM EDT/ Friday the stage was 17.7 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 10.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 7:45 PM CDT /8:45 PM EDT/ Friday was 18.4 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage\ntomorrow evening and continue falling to 4.5 feet Monday,\nSeptember 07.\n- Flood stage is 16.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 17.7\nfeet on 06/12/1980.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nFlooding is occurring. Most flood related deaths occur in\nautomobiles. Do not attempt to cross water covered bridges, dips, or\nlow water crossings. Never try to cross a flowing stream, even a\nsmall one, on foot. To escape rising water find another route over\nhigher ground.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/ind.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Saturday morning at 1015 AM CDT\n/1115 AM EDT/.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSIND"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS83 KIND 290136"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL SUNDAY MORNING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KIND.FL.W.0174.000000T0000Z-260830T1200Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-30T07:00:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cd9499db912cf41eedf6e7ed89ab331259907008.002.1,2026-08-27T20:38:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.