er":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-28T09:43:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-28T20:36:00-05:00","effective":"2026-08-28T20:36:00-05:00","onset":"2026-08-28T20:36:00-05:00","expires":"2026-08-29T10:15:00-05:00","ends":"2026-08-30T11:00:00-05:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Indianapolis IN","headline":"Flood Warning issued August 28 at 8:36PM CDT until August 30 at 11:00AM CDT by NWS Indianapolis IN","description":"...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in\nIndiana...Illinois...\n\nWabash River from Hutsonville to Vincennes.\n\n.Minor flooding continues on the Wabash River from Hutsonville down\nto Vincennes. The river has crested. Flooding should come to an end\non the Wabash over the weekend.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Wabash River at Hutsonville Legacy Power Plant Site.\n\n* WHEN...Until Sunday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 18.0 feet, Seep water occurs behind levees on Indiana\nside.  Hutson Creek begins to overflow from backwater.  Old Darwin\nRoad and a few rural roads in eastern Clark and Crawford counties\nin Illinois are impassable.  Low agricultural land floods.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- There is no current observed data.\n- Bankfull stage is 12.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage late\ntomorrow evening and continue falling to 6.4 feet Monday,\nSeptember 07.\n- Flood stage is 16.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 17.2\nfeet on 06/23/1946.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nFlooding is occurring. Most flood related deaths occur in\nautomobiles. Do not attempt to cross water covered bridges, dips, or\nlow water crossings. Never try to cross a flowing stream, even a\nsmall one, on foot. To escape rising water find another route over\nhigher ground.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/ind.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Saturday morning at 1015 AM CDT\n/1115 AM EDT/.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSIND"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS83 KIND 290136"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL SUNDAY MORNING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KIND.FL.W.0160.000000T0000Z-260830T1600Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-30T11:00:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cd9499db912cf41eedf6e7ed89ab331259907008.003.1,2026-08-27T20:38:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6315cb2dc8d0f54eaa778ad01fb00cd0c181d340.004.1,2026-08-27T10:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.370c270d7d1b162addcf02dc7258854c454ad061.005.1,2026-08-26T13:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.12919d77a71ad3fa4d2d46fe4c889e8395a827c1.007.1,2026-08-26T09:14:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.21fed40f8a4270468743863bc5d2282950a3b72d.008.1,2026-08-25T13:12:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.966efdc66b3086f5aa2b21cb1cfbfa88e06cea31.009.1,2026-08-25T08:35:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.485716edaea873f78d95b8660a4bf26eec3149e1.010.1,2026-08-24T12:54:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d17042b1f0925f697c4f2f6f4a97ea6a0fc7af62.008.1,2026-08-24T20:54:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e611d888f0b860bf842f3076e8bd792348b6b8d0.010.1,2026-08-24T08:54:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.946a70c1dd6536458e250ec5f6d5adee0ba9c93c.003.1,2026-08-23T21:48:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.80aefc3a77c6080a84755a24ef28fd6d4a72367f.009.1,2026-08-23T11:49:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.edbe2de7e5