ek\nDrainage and Levee District.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:45 PM CDT Friday the stage was 14.4 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 7:45 PM CDT Friday was 15.1 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage\ntomorrow evening and continue falling to 11.4 feet Friday,\nSeptember 04.\n- Flood stage is 14.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Persons with interests along this river need to remain aware of the\nlatest forecasts and associated flood risk for their area. Stay tuned\nfor further updates on this flooding situation.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Saturday morning at 900 AM CDT.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSILX"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS83 KILX 290155"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL LATE SATURDAY NIGHT"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KILX.FL.W.0038.000000T0000Z-260830T0600Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-30T01:00:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.668e1ae69338a74e54485f42c8b6cbf9659a53ab.001.1,2026-08-27T20:39:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a53269587bc5b5a7c2a8f154c30a5de1b5bf705b.001.1,2026-08-27T09:48:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e58e572d30a7f9919450eb1ec53c819e613e0e40.001.1,2026-08-26T20:32:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a5ba3eea957db4323b04c5a07c886510d06a1d84.002.1,2026-08-26T09:08:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2ab065555cfd7495a4250782763d80d6b4cd55f3.001.1,2026-08-25T21:42:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d5b0ee461c0617218c6f8ede27b3ea0a66a50e55.001.1,2026-08-25T08:53:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c14f38cf836978ebe82026fa568defb4d55265c9.001.1,2026-08-24T21:28:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,